  "answer": "For May support operations, the Import/OCR ticket count was **112 tickets**, the largest ticket category [NL-029#NL-029-S02]. The documented root cause is that most of these tickets involved image-only or poorly scanned PDF documents lacking native text layers. Because NovaLearn’s ingestion pipeline relies on standard PDF text extraction, such files fail to process, produce garbled text, or generate empty document indexes, and TutorChat may be unable to generate citations [NL-029#NL-029-S02] [NL-029#NL-029-S05].\n\nThe recommended operational response includes developing a **Pre-Ingestion Scanning Tool** in the KnowledgeHub admin dashboard that analyzes uploaded PDFs for text layers and warns users if a file is image-only before it enters the ingestion queue, proactively reducing Import/OCR tickets [NL-029#NL-029-S06]. Additionally, the documented resolution path currently directs support agents to advise customers to run external OCR tools before uploading files, while the permanent resolution requires the release of the Advanced OCR Pipeline planned for August 2026 [NL-029#NL-029-S05].\n\nANSWER_STATUS: answer\nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
